Message Queue
-------------

1. msgget()
2. msgsnd()
3. msgrcv()
4. msgctl()

	msgget() : msgget() is useful for the creating as well as opening the mesage queue
	
	msgsnd() : it is useful for sending the message in to the message queue 

	msgrcv() : it is useful for receiving the message from the message queue 
	
	msgctl() : it is useful for doing some control operation in message queue 


msgget -> get a message queue identifier 

	#include <sys/types.h>
	#include <sys/ipc.h>
	#include <sys/msg.h>

	int msgget(key_t key, int msgflag); // function prototype

	
	1. Key :- Message Queue key 

		The key uniquely identifies a msg queue in the system

		Common key values :

			Key value 		Meaning 

			IPC_PRIVATE		Always create a new unique queue
		
			Any integer key 	Used to access or create a shared queue 

		
		If 2 process use the same key, they can communicate using the same queue

	2. msgflag :- Flags & permssions

		Controls :-
		
			* Whether to create the queue 
			* Access permissions 

		Common flags :- 

			Flag 			Meaning 

			IPC_CREAT		Create queue if it doesn't exist 
			IPC_EXCL		Fail if queue already exist
			0666			Read/write permissions 

	
	Return value :-

		On success : returns message queue ID (msqid)
		On Failure : returns -1 and set errno 

	1. msgget() returns an integer ID that uniquely represents the message queue inside the kernel.

	2. The msgget() system call returns the message queue identifier associated with the value of the key argument 

		if the queue exists :- returns its ID 
		if it doesn't exist and IPC_CREAT is used -> creates and returns ID 
		New message queue create value = IPC_PRIVATE 

			msgget(IPC_PRIVATE, 0666 | IPC_CREAT);

				always creates a new queue
				key is not shared 	
				mostly used between parent-child process (fork)
			     other process can't access this queue using the key 
		
		No message flag (queue) with given key value = IPC_CREAT

			if no queue exists with the given key -> create it 
			if queue exists :- open existing queue 

				Example:- 

					msgget(1234, IPC_CREAT | 0665);
							

	Common msgget() Use cases 

		1. create a new queue (private)
			
			int msqid = msgget(IPC_PRIVATE, 0666 | IPC_CREAT);
			
				New queue	
				unique
				parent-child communication 

		2. Create or Open a shared queue 

			int msqid = msgget(key, IPC_CREAT | 0666);

				Multiple process can accesss
				Used in client-server IPC 
		
		3. Fail if queue already exists 

				msgget(key, IPC_CREAT | IPC_EXCL | 0666);

					Ensure no duplicate queue

		Error Conditions 

			EACCES	 :- permission denied 
			ENOENT   :- Queue does not exist (no IPC_CREAT)
			
		
